## Why This Is Asked

In real-world deployments, fairness during model rollouts matters; quick feedback loops for parity help prevent bias.

## Key Concepts

- Fairness metrics, group parity, drift detection
- Canary rollout, alerting, privacy-preserving logging
- API design for per-group metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example payload for fairness audit
type FairnessEvent = {
  model_version: string;
  group: string;
  cca_score: number;
  baseline_score?: number;
  parity?: number;
  p_value?: number;
  timestamp: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale fairness audits to thousands of groups?
- What privacy controls would you enforce for audit logs?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests API design discipline, latency considerations, and privacy handling for a live scoring service. It requires concrete endpoints, data fields, and rollout strategies rather than abstract concepts.

## Key Concepts
- Deterministic scoring with consistent model behavior across regions
- Privacy-first design with masked user identifiers
- Canary rollout and backpressure mechanisms for safe deployment
- Observability: latency tracking, error monitoring, drift detection

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeScore(features, salt) {
  let h = 0;
  for(const f of features) {
    h = ((h << 5) - h) + f.charCodeAt(0);
    h = h & h;
  }
  return Math.abs(h + salt) % 1000;
}
```

